# Optional: disable Vite hot-module reload during local debugging.
# true = disable HMR, false = keep default behavior.
DISABLE_HMR="false"

# Origin of the brand-motion media site (no trailing slash).
# /motion fetches `${VITE_MOTION_MEDIA_BASE}/manifest.json` in the browser.
# Paths inside the manifest (`video`, `web`, `poster`) are resolved against this origin.
# When `web` is present it is preferred over `video`.
#
# Vite inlines this at build time. Set it in Netlify after the media site is deployed:
#   Site configuration → Environment variables → Add a variable
#   Key:   VITE_MOTION_MEDIA_BASE
#   Value: https://motion.nealfrazier.tech
#   Scopes: Production (and Deploy Previews, if the media host allows them)
# Then trigger a new deploy. Changing the value does not affect an existing build.
#
# The gallery page and the media host are different origins, so the media site must
# allow this site to read manifest.json (Access-Control-Allow-Origin for
# https://www.nealfrazier.tech and https://nealfrazier.tech, or *).
# Leave the variable unset to show the empty state.
#
# Local sample (posters only — do not commit video files):
#   npm run motion:sample
#   VITE_MOTION_MEDIA_BASE=http://127.0.0.1:4174 npm run dev
VITE_MOTION_MEDIA_BASE=https://motion.nealfrazier.tech
